            'Uranus\'s magnetic field is a relic of the ancient giant impact that tilted the planet: the impactor carried its own magnetisation and combined with Uranus\'s original field to produce a permanently tilted and offset configuration; the tilt of 59° is geometrically related to the 97.77° axial tilt because the impact that caused both phenomena struck at the same angle; Neptune\'s similarly exotic field is explained by a separate but contemporaneous impactor from the same population',
